  "caption": "Happiness is an inside job. Getting sober led me back to God, back to myself, and to a kind of peace I spent years looking for everywhere else.\n\nThis past year has taught me that none of the beautiful things on the outside mean much if it doesn’t feel peaceful on the inside. And lately, that inner life is the one I’m most proud of.",
  "transcript": {
    "text": "The more you grow, the less you want. Not less ambition, but less clutter, less noise, less distraction. The things that once seemed urgent, the possessions, the endless chasing, suddenly feel heavy, almost meaningless. You begin to crave simplicity, quiet mornings, gentle routines, moments that feed the soul, not the ego. And then you realize, real wealth has nothing to do with what you hold. It's the peace you carry inside.",
